<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<div>
  Run approval, time-boxed change permissions, and an append-only audit history
  for Jenkins instances that are used as a batch execution manager.
  A manual run of a protected job waits for a designated approver before it
  reaches the queue, and a user without standing permission to create, configure,
  or delete a job can request a time-boxed permission window that adds those
  permissions to what the delegate authorization strategy already grants.
  A window never takes anything away and imposes nothing on users who already
  hold the permission; the only exception is that deleting a job needs an active window while change
  control is on.
  Runs, decisions, configuration changes, and failures are recorded independently
  of build retention, and installing the plugin changes nothing until an
  administrator turns the controls on.
</div>
